1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:06,000
A dental patient, Maria Lopez, asks for every record the practice holds about her.

2
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:12,000
The law gives 30 days. Her data sits in forms, scans, phone photos and voicemails, and her mother has the same name.

3
00:00:12,500 --> 00:00:21,000
On File is a Skill for the NAS assistant. I give it the request type, her name, the date it arrived and the folders.

4
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:29,500
It shows the due date and proposes a case name.

5
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:42,000
It searches file names, document text, text in scans and photos, photo captions, document properties and voicemail recordings,

6
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:54,500
with the NAS's own experts. Nothing is uploaded.

7
00:00:55,000 --> 00:01:07,000
Two intake forms carry her exact name, one born in 1984 and one in 1958, at the same address.

8
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:19,500
It stops and asks which one is the requester's.

9
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:31,000
Every decision keeps its quote and the path of rules that made it.

10
00:01:31,000 --> 00:01:42,000
Her mother's files are excluded, with the line that proves it.

11
00:01:42,000 --> 00:01:54,500
A name with no identifier is never included: it comes to me, with the evidence for and against.

12
00:01:55,000 --> 00:02:05,000
Files that also hold other patients become extracts of her own entries.

13
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:14,500
The letter and the list of records name no one else.

14
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:39,500
In act mode, each copy is its own approval, and every action goes into an audit log with checksums.

15
00:02:40,000 --> 00:02:49,500
At the end it checks that every file it did not touch is unchanged. Search, decisions, letter: all on the NAS.

16
00:02:50,000 --> 00:02:59,000
On File.
